WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.234
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.979
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.279 --> 00:00:16.691
Unit twenty-three: Innovation and Inventions. Today you will talk about inventions with the past passive.

4
00:00:16.991 --> 00:00:19.736
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.409
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.309
Invention.

7
00:00:27.317 --> 00:00:30.303
Invention means a new thing that someone creates.

8
00:00:30.917 --> 00:00:32.986
The light bulb was a great invention.

9
00:00:33.583 --> 00:00:36.027
Your turn. Say: Invention.

10
00:00:38.867 --> 00:00:39.879
Invention.

11
00:00:40.617 --> 00:00:41.618
Innovation.

12
00:00:42.617 --> 00:00:45.998
Innovation means a new idea or way of doing something.

13
00:00:46.583 --> 00:00:48.618
Mobile banking is an innovation.

14
00:00:49.217 --> 00:00:51.544
Your turn. Say: Innovation.

15
00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.401
Innovation.

16
00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:57.221
Inventor.

17
00:00:58.217 --> 00:01:01.017
Inventor means a person who creates something new.

18
00:01:01.617 --> 00:01:03.419
The inventor worked for years.

19
00:01:04.017 --> 00:01:06.623
Your turn. Say: Inventor.

20
00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:10.630
Inventor.

21
00:01:11.383 --> 00:01:12.361
Design.

22
00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:16.104
Design means to plan how something will look and work.

23
00:01:16.717 --> 00:01:18.589
She designed a new water filter.

24
00:01:19.183 --> 00:01:22.079
Your turn. Say: Design.

25
00:01:24.933 --> 00:01:26.027
Design.

26
00:01:26.783 --> 00:01:27.610
Problem.

27
00:01:28.617 --> 00:01:31.661
Problem means something difficult that needs a solution.

28
00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.959
Dirty water is a big problem.

29
00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:36.912
Your turn. Say: Problem.

30
00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:40.617
Problem.

31
00:01:41.383 --> 00:01:42.315
Solution.

32
00:01:43.317 --> 00:01:45.711
Solution means a way to solve a problem.

33
00:01:46.317 --> 00:01:48.374
Solar lamps are a cheap solution.

34
00:01:48.983 --> 00:01:51.369
Your turn. Say: Solution.

35
00:01:54.233 --> 00:01:55.200
Solution.

36
00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:56.986
Technology.

37
00:01:57.983 --> 00:02:01.051
Technology means machines and tools made with science.

38
00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:03.882
Technology changes very fast.

39
00:02:04.483 --> 00:02:07.112
Your turn. Say: Technology.

40
00:02:09.967 --> 00:02:11.107
Technology.

41
00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:13.037
Improve.

42
00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:15.968
Improve means to make better.

43
00:02:16.583 --> 00:02:18.490
Phones are improved every year.

44
00:02:19.083 --> 00:02:21.770
Your turn. Say: Improve.

45
00:02:24.633 --> 00:02:25.600
Improve.

46
00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.853
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:33.599
Visal, which invention changed the world the most?

48
00:02:34.683 --> 00:02:40.436
I think the telephone. It was invented in the 1870s.

49
00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:42.470
And now?

50
00:02:43.583 --> 00:02:48.325
Smartphones were designed later. They were improved again and again.

51
00:02:49.417 --> 00:02:50.987
What problem did they solve?

52
00:02:52.083 --> 00:02:56.442
Distance! Now people are connected everywhere.

53
00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.112
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:03.041
Grammar focus: Passive voice (was invented).

55
00:03:03.341 --> 00:03:04.702
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:05.417 --> 00:03:08.937
The telephone was invented in the 1870s.

57
00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:12.198
Smartphones were designed to connect people.

58
00:03:13.083 --> 00:03:15.559
The light bulb was improved by Edison.

59
00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.987
Use 'was' for one thing and 'were' for more than one thing.

60
00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:25.061
Be careful! Don't say: The telephone invented in the 1870s.

61
00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:31.333
Say: The telephone was invented in the 1870s.

62
00:03:31.633 --> 00:03:34.979
The past passive is 'was' or 'were' + past participle.

63
00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:38.419
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:39.233 --> 00:03:40.896
From Problem to Solution.

65
00:03:41.196 --> 00:03:43.405
Every invention starts with a problem.

66
00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.365
An inventor designs a solution.

67
00:03:47.367 --> 00:03:51.026
The telephone was invented in the 1870s.

68
00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:54.532
It was improved by innovation over many years.

69
00:03:55.533 --> 00:03:59.170
Today, technology like the smartphone has changed how we live.

70
00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:04.164
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:05.017 --> 00:04:08.630
The telephone blank invented in the 1870s.

72
00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:11.806
A, was. B, were. C, is been.

73
00:04:15.367 --> 00:04:17.540
The answer is A: was.

74
00:04:18.683 --> 00:04:21.252
A person who creates something new is an blank.

75
00:04:21.552 --> 00:04:25.530
A, inventor. B, invention. C, innovation.

76
00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:30.880
The answer is A: inventor.

77
00:04:32.017 --> 00:04:34.086
A way to solve a problem is a blank.

78
00:04:34.386 --> 00:04:38.515
A, solution. B, design. C, technology.

79
00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:44.229
The answer is A: solution.

80
00:04:45.433 --> 00:04:48.515
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:51.802
Which invention changed the world the most?

82
00:05:00.617 --> 00:05:01.989
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:05:02.289 --> 00:05:12.117
I think the internet changed the world the most. It was developed for scientists, but now it is used by billions of people every day.

84
00:05:12.417 --> 00:05:14.161
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:19.502
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and passive voice (was invented).

86
00:05:19.802 --> 00:05:23.673
Today's value is creativity. Use your imagination when you play.

87
00:05:23.973 --> 00:05:26.951
See you in Unit twenty-four. Goodbye!

88
00:05:27.251 --> 00:05:29.984
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

